other systems

Windows

    Import the Certificate to the Trusted Root Certification Authorities Store:
        Open the Certificate Management Tool:
            Press Win + R, type certmgr.msc, and press Enter to open the Certificate Manager.
        Navigate to Trusted Root Certification Authorities:
            In the left pane, expand Certificates - Current User or Certificates (Local Computer) (for all users).
            Right-click Trusted Root Certification Authorities > All Tasks > Import.
        Import the Certificate:
            Click Next in the Certificate Import Wizard.
            Browse to your server.crt file and select it.
            Ensure the certificate is placed in the Trusted Root Certification Authorities store.
            Complete the wizard and click Finish.
        Restart the Browser

Linux (Ubuntu/Debian)

    Add the Certificate to the System Trust Store:
        Copy the Certificate:
            Copy your server.crt to the system’s certificate store:
            bash

    sudo cp server.crt /usr/local/share/ca-certificates/

    Update the Certificate Store:

    Run the following command to update the system’s trusted certificates:
    bash

    sudo update-ca-certificates
    This adds the certificate to /etc/ssl/certs.

    Restart the Browser

Firefox-Specific Steps (All Operating Systems)

    Firefox maintains its own certificate store, independent of the OS.

    Import the Certificate in Firefox:
        Open Firefox and go to Settings > Privacy & Security.
        Scroll to the Certificates section and click View Certificates.
        In the Certificate Manager, go to the Authorities tab and click Import.
        Select your server.crt file and click Open.
        Check the box for Trust this CA to identify websites and click OK.
        Restart Firefox.

Mobile Browsers

    iOS (Safari):
        Email or transfer server.crt to your iOS device.
        Open the file on the device, which prompts installation.
        Go to Settings > General > Profile > [Your Certificate] > Install.
        Enable trust: Go to Settings > General > About > Certificate Trust Settings and toggle on trust for your certificate.

Android (Chrome):

    Transfer server.crt to your device.
    Go to Settings > Security > Install from storage (or similar, depending on the Android version).
    Select server.crt and install it as a CA certificate.


